maya: Hey team — I'm going to refresh the quickstart 'hello-world' onboarding to use ephemeral API keys + a tiny GH Actions example that mints at workflow runtime. This should replace the legacy env-var approach and the docker-compose auth example. Will update docs/quickstart/hello-world.md, snippets/auth.md, and samples/hello-world. Any blockers?

jordan: sounds good. one request: keep a single-file minimal example for copy/paste (people paste the whole thing). The current multi-file example confuses newcomers.

li: also flag for eng-security: we need a one-line "Do not log tokens" callout in the runtime examples. Ops saw people accidentally echo envs in logs.

maya: yes — I'll add a Security notes mini-section and a short checklist. Sam, can you help with the GH Actions step that requests ephemeral tokens from the internal mint service?

sam: sure. suggested flow: runner hits /mint with a short-lived job credential, receives token, writes to GITHUB_ENV for the step, then uses it in deployment step. I'll draft a compact action snippet.

maya: posting a tiny node helper for rotation and cleanup (docs-only):
```js
// docs/snippets/ephemeral-rotation.js
function startRotation(getToken, apply) {
  let timer = null;
  let stopped = false;
  async function tick() {
    if (stopped) return;
    const t = await getToken();
    apply(t);
    timer = setTimeout(tick, 50 * 60 * 1000); // refresh before expiry
  }
  tick();
  return { stop: () => { stopped = true; clearTimeout(timer); } };
}
module.exports = { startRotation };
```

jordan: nice. add a single-line comment about not calling getToken on every request (cache it). Also mention tests should stub getToken.

li: small ask: include a short migration snippet for Dedicated/private explaining how to adapt the mint step to use customer KMS/HSM signing (one sentence + link to infra runbook).

