sam: GH Actions snippet draft (compact):
```yaml
- name: Mint ephemeral key
  run: |
    curl -sS -X POST $MINT_URL -H "Authorization: Bearer $JOB_TOKEN" -d '{"purpose":"docs-demo"}' \
      | jq -r .token >> $GITHUB_ENV
- name: Use token
  env:
    REDWOOD_API_KEY: ${{ env.token }}
  run: node deploy.js
```

(note: this is intentionally minimal for docs; link to a full workflow in samples)

jordan: please use $GITHUB_ENV append semantics correctly — our example should show how to write the variable name, and don't forget to show reading it in next step as ${{ env.REDWOOD_API_KEY }}. small nit.

sam: good catch, I'll fix that before PR.

